cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper (in preparation)."

title: "RITS: Range–Intensity Thresholding with Zero-Intensity Surface Suppression for Training-Free Snow Removal in Spinning LiDAR"

abstract: >-
  RITS detects and removes snowfall-induced noise from mechanical spinning
  LiDAR point clouds per point, at frame rate, on CPU, without training, GPU or
  learned weights. The method combines a smooth range-intensity threshold whose
  distance dependence is a Gamma-shaped fit to the weather-particle range
  distribution, a per-point intensity score fused with a normalised
  height-above-ground term, and a zero-intensity surface veto that rejects points
  attached to a bright surface. The algorithm core is ROS-agnostic and ships as a
  library with an offline CLI; a separate ROS 2 package wraps it as a point-cloud
  node. Both paths produce bit-identical detections, which is enforced by a
  byte-exact regression against a released reference output.

authors:
